---
/**
 * /about - who makes WakeSharp and how its articles are held to account.
 *
 * English only, like the legal bodies: the "Reviewed by" line under each
 * reviewed post links here from every language. It names only what the owner
 * chose to publish (name, role, company) and invents no credentials; the
 * editorial standards describe the checks the site actually runs.
 */
import { refreshCopy } from '../lib/refresh';
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { PEOPLE, personId } from '../config/people';

const founder = PEOPLE.founder;
const orgId = `${SITE.url}/#org`;
const pageUrl = new URL('/about', SITE.url).href;

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'AboutPage',
      '@id': pageUrl,
      url: pageUrl,
      name: 'About WakeSharp',
      isPartOf: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#website` },
      about: { '@id': orgId },
      mainEntity: { '@id': orgId },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      '@id': orgId,
      name: SITE.publisher,
      url: SITE.url,
      email: SITE.email,
      logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: new URL('/icon-512.png', SITE.url).href, width: 512, height: 512 },
      address: { '@type': 'PostalAddress', addressLocality: 'Manotick', addressRegion: 'ON', addressCountry: 'CA' },
      founder: { '@id': personId('founder', SITE.url) },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'Person',
      '@id': personId('founder', SITE.url),
      name: founder.name,
      jobTitle: founder.jobTitle,
      url: pageUrl,
      worksFor: { '@id': orgId },
    },
  ],
};
---

<LegalLayout
  title="About WakeSharp - Who Makes It and How We Write"
  description="WakeSharp is made by KineticBit Inc., a small independent studio in Ontario, Canada. Who reviews the articles, how they cite research, and how to reach us."
  path="/about"
  heading="About WakeSharp"
  intro="I’m Dipojjal, the developer behind WakeSharp. I build an alarm clock with missions, loud tones and tools for planning your mornings at KineticBit in Ontario, Canada."
  showUpdated={false}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />

  <p>{refreshCopy('en').developer}</p>
  <h2>Who makes WakeSharp</h2>
  <p>
    WakeSharp is made by {SITE.publisher}, a small independent studio in Manotick, Ontario, Canada, which
    publishes both the iPhone and the Android app. The company is the publisher of every article on this
    site.
  </p>

  <h2 id={founder.anchor}>{founder.name}</h2>
  <p>
    {founder.name} is the founder of WakeSharp at {SITE.publisher}, and reviews the articles on this site
    that carry the line “Reviewed by {founder.name}”.
  </p>

  <h2>How the articles are written</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Every claim about sleep cites its source.</strong> Articles link to the studies, reviews and official guidance they rely on, so you can read the evidence yourself rather than take our word for it.</li>
    <li><strong>“Reviewed by” means a named person read it.</strong> A post shows a reviewer only when that person has read it, and the structured data records the date they did.</li>
    <li><strong>Claims about the app are checked against the app.</strong> Anything an article says WakeSharp does has to match the stated release, with previews labeled, and the site’s own checks reject the claims the app has retired.</li>
    <li><strong>Corrections are dated.</strong> When an article changes in substance, it shows an “Updated” date. If you find a mistake, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and I will check it.</li>
    <li><strong>It is not medical advice.</strong> The articles are general information about sleep and waking up. For a sleep problem that persists, talk to a clinician.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>For writers</h2><p>The <a href="/press">press kit</a> has product facts, submitted screenshots and release notes for independent coverage.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>, use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>, or see
    <a href="/support">Support</a> for the questions that come up most.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
